from ./OutputSize import OutputSize
from ./SvgOutput import SvgOutput

export anchor PngOutput:
    description:
        How a composition is turned into PNG. The PNG is the SVG output
        rasterized, described in @{SvgOutput}. It is never laid out or drawn
        separately, so it always matches the SVG.

    files:
        Each rendered composition becomes one PNG file in the output
        directory, named after the composition, such as `MyComposition.png`.

    source:
        The PNG is rasterized from the SVG with text in outline form,
        whatever the SVG fonts option is set to. Embedded fonts never affect
        the PNG.

    size:
        The image is the output size multiplied by the scale, as described in
        @{OutputSize}, in whole pixels. A scale of `2` gives an image twice as
        wide and twice as tall, with every shape drawn at the higher
        resolution, not stretched.

    pixels:
        Pixels are 8-bit RGBA in the sRGB colour space. Edges are
        anti-aliased.

    transparency:
        Transparency is kept. Where nothing is drawn and no canvas background
        is set, pixels are fully transparent.

    metadata:
        The PNG holds no metadata beyond what the format needs, so the same
        input always produces the same file, byte for byte.
